---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FeatureArticle from './editorial/FeatureArticle.astro';
import ArticleOpening from './editorial/ArticleOpening.astro';
import ArticleFigure from './editorial/ArticleFigure.astro';
import ArticlePullQuote from './editorial/ArticlePullQuote.astro';
import Study from '../previews/spacewar/study.mdx';
import MovingShot from '../previews/spacewar/moving-shot.mdx';
import DuelDesign from '../previews/spacewar/duel-design.mdx';
import CaptureCredits from '../previews/spacewar/capture-credits.mdx';
import source from '../previews/spacewar/source.json';
import {gameStudies, studyPath, GAME_STUDIES_ROOT} from '../data/game-studies.mjs';
export interface Props { page?: string; }
const slug=Astro.props.page;
const study=gameStudies.find(study=>study.slug==='spacewar')!;
const root=studyPath(study.slug);
const pages={
 'moving-shot':{component:MovingShot,title:'Shooting from a moving ship',description:'Why a shot can travel somewhere other than where the launcher points.'},
 'duel-design':{component:DuelDesign,title:'What makes a duel worth another go?',description:'Resources, commitment and counterplay inside a very small world.'},
 'capture-credits':{component:CaptureCredits,title:'Capture credits and provenance',description:'The edition, conditions and people behind the three game frames in this study.'},
};
const isStudy=!slug;
const isSpecimen=slug==='specimen';
const selected=pages[slug as keyof typeof pages];
const Content=selected?.component ?? Study;
const title=isStudy?'Spacewar!':isSpecimen?'A movement problem you can see':selected.title;
const description=isStudy?'Two ships, one star, and a universe of things to discover about games.':isSpecimen?'A second composition using the same article structures, without a picture behind the title.':selected.description;
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'The Vault',href:'/vault/'},{label:'Game studies',href:GAME_STUDIES_ROOT},{label:'Spacewar!',href:isStudy?undefined:root},...(isStudy?[]:[{label:title}])];
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} masthead={false} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} breadcrumbPlacement="article" noindex={!study.reviewed || isSpecimen}>
 <FeatureArticle>
  <ArticleOpening slot="opening" title={title} subtitle={isStudy?'A universe worth playing in':undefined} description={description} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} image={isStudy?'/images/studies/spacewar/header-2172.webp':undefined} imageSet={isStudy?'/images/studies/spacewar/header-1280.webp 1280w, /images/studies/spacewar/header-2172.webp 2172w':undefined} imageCredit={isStudy?'Original editorial illustration · game captures below':undefined} metadata={isStudy?'PDP-1 · 1962 · Whole-game study':undefined} tone={isStudy?'ink':'paper'} />
  {isSpecimen ? <>
   <p>A movement diagram gives us something to point at. We can separate a ship's heading from its velocity, then add the change from thrust and see why it travels in a new direction.</p>
   <h2>One change at a time</h2>
   <p>The orange arrow shows a change in velocity. Adding it to the blue arrow gives the green result. Those arrows describe motion; they do not draw the path the ship will follow.</p>
   <ArticleFigure src="/images/studies/spacewar/figures/thrust.svg" alt="A rightward velocity and an upward change combine into a diagonal velocity." width={640} height={360} caption="Original explanatory diagram. The engine adds to the motion already present; it does not replace it." size="reading" />
   <ArticlePullQuote text="The engine adds to the motion already present; it does not replace it." duplicate={true} />
   <h2>Keep the evidence in view</h2>
   <p>A capture and a diagram answer different questions. The capture lets us inspect the game display. The diagram isolates a relationship so that we can follow it.</p>
   <ArticleFigure src="/images/studies/spacewar/captures/opening.png" alt="The Needle and Wedge ships on opposite sides of the central star in Spacewar 3.1." width={512} height={512} caption="Spacewar! 3.1 (MIT contributors, 1962, PDP-1), self-captured in Norbert Landsteiner's browser emulator. This is an emulator frame, not a photograph of a CRT." size="bleed" pixels />
   <p><a href={root}>Read the full Spacewar study</a> or <a href={studyPath(study.slug,'capture-credits')}>check capture credits</a>.</p>
  </> : <Content />}
  <Fragment slot="ending">
   <p>This study has not yet been fact-checked. Sources and capture conditions are included so you can follow the evidence.</p>
   <p>Game captures: <em>Spacewar!</em>, MIT contributors, 1962, PDP-1; captured in Norbert Landsteiner's emulator. <a href={studyPath(study.slug,'capture-credits')}>Full credits and capture conditions</a>. Original illustration is separate from the historical game imagery.</p>
   <p><a href={source.canonical}>Study sources and research notes</a> · <a href={GAME_STUDIES_ROOT}>More game studies</a></p>
  </Fragment>
 </FeatureArticle>
</Layout>
